IMPORT prelude

-- Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966 (Singapore) -- the rules an ordinary Muslim, employer or wedding party meets: employer
-- contributions to the Mosque Building and Mendaki Fund and the employee's opt-out (ss 78, 79, Third Schedule); halal certification
-- offences (s 88A(5)); who may solemnise a marriage and when (ss 94B, 95, 96, 97, Fourth Schedule); the 7-day duty to attend the
-- Syariah Court after a divorce (ss 102(5), 130(2)); and the offences of Part 9 (ss 129 to 140).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/AMLA1966.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 4 of 2024 (latest commencement annotated: 01/10/2025) and Act 5 of 2025 (wef 09/03/2025) shown. The Third Schedule amounts
-- carry the annotation S 144/2016.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the duties, offences and thresholds
-- above. Not encoded: the Majlis and its constitution (Part 2), the Syariah Court's jurisdiction and procedure, divorce grounds and
-- ancillary orders (ss 46A to 56B), wakaf, nazar and zakat administration, mosques and religious schools beyond the Fund, Haj
-- regulation, appeals (Part 5B), the betrothal claim (s 94), the marriage preparation programme (s 94A, whose class is set by rules),
-- registration mechanics other than s 102(5), inheritance and property (Part 7), conversions other than the duty to report, and
-- Part 10.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966 -- obligations`

§§ `78, 79 and Third Schedule -- Mosque Building and Mendaki Fund`

-- s 78(1): "every employer of a Muslim employee must pay to the Mosque Building and Mendaki Fund monthly in respect of each Muslim
-- employee contributions as set out in the Third Schedule"; (2) the employer may recover them from the employee's monthly wages.
-- Third Schedule (S 144/2016), by the employee's total wages for the calendar month:
--   not more than $1,000 -- $3;  $1,000 to $2,000 -- $4.50;  $2,000 to $3,000 -- $6.50;  $3,000 to $4,000 -- $15;
--   $4,000 to $6,000 -- $19.50;  $6,000 to $8,000 -- $22;  $8,000 to $10,000 -- $24;  more than $10,000 -- $26.
-- (Each band is "More than [lower] but not more than [upper]".)
GIVEN `wages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly MBMF contribution` MEANS
        3
    PLUS `the step` `wages` 1000 (3 DIVIDED BY 2)
    PLUS `the step` `wages` 2000 2
    PLUS `the step` `wages` 3000 (17 DIVIDED BY 2)
    PLUS `the step` `wages` 4000 (9 DIVIDED BY 2)
    PLUS `the step` `wages` 6000 (5 DIVIDED BY 2)
    PLUS `the step` `wages` 8000 2
    PLUS `the step` `wages` 10000 2

-- Written as a running total of the increase at each band edge ($3, then +$1.50, +$2, +$8.50, +$4.50, +$2.50, +$2, +$2), because
-- a long ELSE IF chain would not parse; the cases test every band value against the Schedule directly.
GIVEN `wages` IS A NUMBER, `edge` IS A NUMBER, `increase` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the step` MEANS
    IF `wages` GREATER THAN `edge` THEN `increase` ELSE 0

-- s 79(1): a Muslim employee "who does not wish his or her employer to pay contributions" may exercise an option; (2) the Majlis
-- issues a certificate; (3) on notice, "the employer ceases to be liable ... for such period the certificate is in force"; (4)
-- liability revives when the certificate expires unless a fresh one is issued. The contribution is opt-out, not opt-in.
GIVEN `the employee is a Muslim` IS A BOOLEAN, `an opt-out certificate is in force and the employer notified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer must contribute` IF
    `the employee is a Muslim` AND (NOT `an opt-out certificate is in force and the employer notified`)

-- s 78(3): failing to pay within the prescribed time -- fine up to $500. (4): an employer who "has recovered any amount from the
-- monthly wages" and fails to pay it over -- fine up to $2,000. (The prescribed time is in rules, not the Act.)
GIVEN `paid within the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN, `deducted it from the wages` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the employer's maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `paid within the prescribed time` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `deducted it from the wages` THEN 2000 ELSE 500

§§ `88A(5) -- halal certificates and marks`

-- s 88A(5): any person who, "without the approval of the Majlis", (a) issues a halal certificate, or (b) uses any specified halal
-- certification mark "or any colourable imitation thereof", commits an offence -- $10,000 or 12 months or both. Not in Part 9, so
-- not limited to Muslims by s 129.
GIVEN `issued a halal certificate` IS A BOOLEAN, `used the mark or an imitation` IS A BOOLEAN, `had Majlis approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the halal offence is committed` IF
    (`issued a halal certificate` OR `used the mark or an imitation`) AND (NOT `had Majlis approval`)

§§ `95 and 96 -- who may solemnise`

-- s 95(1): a marriage may be solemnised (a) by the wali; (b) by a Kadi or Naib Kadi "at the request of the wali"; or (c) by a Kadi
-- where (i) there is no wali or (ii) the wali refuses consent "on grounds that the Kadi does not consider satisfactory".
-- (2): from 22 October 2018 a wali can solemnise only if (a) a Kadi or Naib Kadi has given written consent and (b) a Kadi or Naib
-- Kadi is present.
-- s 96(2): if the man "is married to any person other than the other party", only (a) a Kadi, or (b) the wali with the written
-- consent of a Kadi -- a Naib Kadi cannot.
-- s 96(4): no marriage if "either party is below 18 years of age"; (5) "Despite subsection (4), a Kadi may in special circumstances
-- solemnise the marriage of a girl who is below 18 years of age but has attained the age of puberty". There is no matching
-- exception for a man below 18, and only a Kadi -- not a Naib Kadi, not the wali -- may use it.
DECLARE Solemniser IS ONE OF
    `the wali`
    `a Kadi`
    `a Naib Kadi`

DECLARE Wedding
    HAS `there is a wali` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the wali requests a Kadi or Naib Kadi` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the wali refuses on grounds the Kadi finds unsatisfactory` IS A BOOLEAN
        `written consent of a Kadi or Naib Kadi for the wali` IS A BOOLEAN
        `written consent of a Kadi for the wali` IS A BOOLEAN
        `a Kadi or Naib Kadi is present` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the man is already married to someone else` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the man is below 18` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the woman is below 18` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the woman has attained puberty` IS A BOOLEAN
        `a Kadi finds special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `who` IS A Solemniser, `w` IS A Wedding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 95 authorises the solemniser` IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `the wali` THEN `w`'s `there is a wali` AND `w`'s `written consent of a Kadi or Naib Kadi for the wali` AND `w`'s `a Kadi or Naib Kadi is present`
    WHEN `a Naib Kadi` THEN `w`'s `the wali requests a Kadi or Naib Kadi`
    WHEN `a Kadi` THEN `w`'s `the wali requests a Kadi or Naib Kadi` OR (NOT `w`'s `there is a wali`) OR `w`'s `the wali refuses on grounds the Kadi finds unsatisfactory`

GIVEN `who` IS A Solemniser, `w` IS A Wedding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 96(2) is satisfied` IF
    IF `w`'s `the man is already married to someone else`
    THEN CONSIDER `who`
         WHEN `a Kadi` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the wali` THEN `w`'s `written consent of a Kadi for the wali`
         WHEN `a Naib Kadi` THEN FALSE
    ELSE TRUE

GIVEN `who` IS A Solemniser, `w` IS A Wedding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the age rule is satisfied` IF
        (NOT `w`'s `the man is below 18`)
    AND (    (NOT `w`'s `the woman is below 18`)
         OR  (`who` EQUALS `a Kadi` AND `w`'s `the woman has attained puberty` AND `w`'s `a Kadi finds special circumstances`))

GIVEN `who` IS A Solemniser, `w` IS A Wedding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the solemniser may proceed` IF
    `s 95 authorises the solemniser` `who` `w` AND `s 96(2) is satisfied` `who` `w` AND `the age rule is satisfied` `who` `w`

§§ `97 -- marriage of a janda`

-- s 2: "janda" means a female who has been married and whose marriage has been terminated by divorce or the death of her husband.
-- s 97(1): (a) she must not be married "to any person other than the husband from whom she was last divorced" before the iddah
-- expires; (b) she must first produce a death certificate, divorce certificate, certified register entry, or a Syariah Court
-- certificate that she is a janda; (c) "if the divorce was by 3 talak, she must not be remarried to her previous husband, unless
-- prior to the marriage she has been lawfully married to some other person and such marriage has been consummated and later
-- lawfully dissolved". The iddah bar does not apply to remarrying the last husband.
DECLARE Janda
    HAS `marrying the husband she was last divorced from` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the iddah has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
        `has produced a qualifying certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the divorce was by 3 talak` IS A BOOLEAN
        `an intervening marriage was consummated and dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `j` IS A Janda
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the janda may be married` IF
        (`j`'s `marrying the husband she was last divorced from` OR `j`'s `the iddah has expired`)
    AND `j`'s `has produced a qualifying certificate`
    AND (    (NOT `j`'s `marrying the husband she was last divorced from`)
         OR  (NOT `j`'s `the divorce was by 3 talak`)
         OR  `j`'s `an intervening marriage was consummated and dissolved`)

§§ `94B and Fourth Schedule -- consent for the marriage of a minor`

-- s 94B(1): no application to a Kadi or Naib Kadi to solemnise "the marriage of a minor without the consent of the appropriate
-- person or persons mentioned in the Fourth Schedule". The Act as deposited does not define "minor" in s 2 (not encoded).
-- Fourth Schedule Part 1 (legitimate minor): parents living together -- both parents; divorced or separated -- the parent with
-- custody, or both if custody is joint or split by period; one parent deserted -- the deserted parent; both deprived of custody by
-- court order -- the person with custody by court order; one parent dead and no other guardian -- the surviving parent; both dead --
-- the guardians appointed by the parents or the court under the Guardianship of Infants Act 1934.
-- Part 2 (illegitimate minor): mother alive -- the mother, or if she has been deprived of custody by court order the person with
-- custody; mother dead -- the guardian appointed by the mother or the court. The father's consent is not required under Part 2.
-- (Part 1 item 2(b), one parent dead with a guardian appointed by that parent, is not encoded.)
DECLARE MinorSituation IS ONE OF
    `legitimate, parents living together`
    `legitimate, parents divorced, custody to one parent`
    `legitimate, parents divorced, custody to both`
    `legitimate, one parent deserted by the other`
    `legitimate, both parents deprived of custody by court`
    `legitimate, one parent dead, no other guardian`
    `legitimate, both parents dead`
    `illegitimate, mother alive with custody`
    `illegitimate, mother alive but deprived of custody by court`
    `illegitimate, mother dead`

DECLARE Consenter IS ONE OF
    `both parents`
    `the parent with custody`
    `the deserted parent`
    `the person given custody by court order`
    `the surviving parent`
    `the appointed guardians`
    `the mother`

GIVEN `situation` IS A MinorSituation
GIVETH A Consenter
`whose consent is required` MEANS
    CONSIDER `situation`
    WHEN `legitimate, parents living together` THEN `both parents`
    WHEN `legitimate, parents divorced, custody to one parent` THEN `the parent with custody`
    WHEN `legitimate, parents divorced, custody to both` THEN `both parents`
    WHEN `legitimate, one parent deserted by the other` THEN `the deserted parent`
    WHEN `legitimate, both parents deprived of custody by court` THEN `the person given custody by court order`
    WHEN `legitimate, one parent dead, no other guardian` THEN `the surviving parent`
    WHEN `legitimate, both parents dead` THEN `the appointed guardians`
    WHEN `illegitimate, mother alive with custody` THEN `the mother`
    WHEN `illegitimate, mother alive but deprived of custody by court` THEN `the person given custody by court order`
    WHEN `illegitimate, mother dead` THEN `the appointed guardians`

-- s 94B(2): where an appropriate person's consent "cannot be obtained by reason of that person being absent, inaccessible or under
-- any disability", the Kadi or Naib Kadi (a) MUST dispense with it "if the consent of any other person is required", and (b) MAY
-- dispense "if the consent of no other person is required". (3), (4): a refusal may be dispensed with on application, after the
-- refuser is given an opportunity to show cause.
GIVEN `consent unobtainable through absence or disability` IS A BOOLEAN, `another person's consent is also required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Kadi must dispense with the consent` IF
    `consent unobtainable through absence or disability` AND `another person's consent is also required`

GIVEN `consent unobtainable through absence or disability` IS A BOOLEAN, `the refuser was given a chance to show cause` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Kadi may dispense with the consent` IF
        `consent unobtainable through absence or disability`
    OR  (`the person refused` AND `the refuser was given a chance to show cause`)

§§ `102(5) and 130(2) -- attending the Syariah Court after a divorce`

-- s 102(5): "In the case of every divorce effected in Singapore, the husband and wife must attend personally at the Syariah Court
-- within 7 days beginning on the date of the divorce, or such extended time as the Syariah Court thinks fit". s 130(2): contravening
-- s 102(5) -- fine up to $500.
-- INFERENCE: "within 7 days beginning on the date of the divorce" is read as the date of divorce counting as day 1, so attendance on
-- the 6th day after that date is the last day in time.
GIVEN `days after the divorce date` IS A NUMBER, `within an extension granted by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the attendance is in time` IF
    `days after the divorce date` AT MOST 6 OR `within an extension granted by the Court`

§§ `129 to 140 -- offences`

-- s 129: "Subject to this Act, this Part only applies to Muslims."
-- s 130(1) omitting to register a marriage or revocation of divorce in time -- $500; (2) s 102(5) -- $500.
-- s 131 not handing over a register book or seal -- $500 or 6 months; s 132 unlawful register or certificate -- $500 or 6 months;
-- s 133 unlawful solemnisation or registration -- $500 or 6 months.
-- s 134(1), (2): a man or a woman who "cohabits and lives with" someone, "whether a Muslim or not", to whom they are not lawfully
-- married -- $500 or 6 months; (3) a woman may instead be detained "in a place of safety" for up to 12 months.
-- s 135 taking or enticing an unmarried woman from her wali without consent -- imprisonment up to 3 years "and shall also be liable
-- to a fine" (no maximum stated).
-- s 137(1) refusing or wilfully failing to pay zakat -- $500 or 6 months; (2) fitrah -- $50 or one month; (3) conviction does not
-- extinguish the debt.
-- s 138 wilfully failing to report a conversion -- $500 or 6 months; s 139 false doctrine -- $2,000 or 12 months.
-- s 140: attempt or abetment -- the same punishment.
-- Outside Part 9 (not limited to Muslims by s 129): s 78(3) $500; s 78(4) $2,000; s 88A(5) $10,000 or 12 months.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 78(3) late Fund contributions`
    `s 78(4) deducted Fund contributions not paid over`
    `s 88A(5) unapproved halal certificate or mark`
    `s 130 failing to register in time`
    `s 131 keeping a register book or seal`
    `s 132 unlawful register or certificate`
    `s 133 unlawful solemnisation or registration`
    `s 134 cohabitation outside marriage`
    `s 135 enticing an unmarried woman from her wali`
    `s 137(1) not paying zakat`
    `s 137(2) not paying fitrah`
    `s 138 not reporting a conversion`
    `s 139 false doctrine`

GIVEN `o` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is in Part 9` IF
    CONSIDER `o`
    WHEN `s 78(3) late Fund contributions` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 78(4) deducted Fund contributions not paid over` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 88A(5) unapproved halal certificate or mark` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `o` IS A Offence, `the accused is a Muslim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence can apply to the accused` IF
    `the accused is a Muslim` OR (NOT `the offence is in Part 9` `o`)

-- Maximum fine in dollars; -1 stands for "liable to a fine" with no maximum stated (s 135).
GIVEN `o` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o`
    WHEN `s 78(3) late Fund contributions` THEN 500
    WHEN `s 78(4) deducted Fund contributions not paid over` THEN 2000
    WHEN `s 88A(5) unapproved halal certificate or mark` THEN 10000
    WHEN `s 130 failing to register in time` THEN 500
    WHEN `s 135 enticing an unmarried woman from her wali` THEN -1
    WHEN `s 137(2) not paying fitrah` THEN 50
    WHEN `s 139 false doctrine` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 500

GIVEN `o` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o`
    WHEN `s 78(3) late Fund contributions` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 78(4) deducted Fund contributions not paid over` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 130 failing to register in time` THEN 0
    WHEN `s 88A(5) unapproved halal certificate or mark` THEN 12
    WHEN `s 135 enticing an unmarried woman from her wali` THEN 36
    WHEN `s 137(2) not paying fitrah` THEN 1
    WHEN `s 139 false doctrine` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 6

-- s 134: both partners commit the offence, but by s 129 only a Muslim partner can be liable; s 134(3) gives the court a
-- place-of-safety alternative for a woman only.
GIVEN `cohabiting with someone not lawfully married to` IS A BOOLEAN, `this partner is a Muslim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this partner commits the cohabitation offence` IF
    `cohabiting with someone not lawfully married to` AND `this partner is a Muslim`

GIVEN `the offender is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the place-of-safety order is available` IF
    `the offender is a woman`

-- s 139(2): "where evidence is given by the Mufti that any doctrine, ceremony or act is contrary to the Muslim law, the court is to
-- presume that such doctrine, ceremony or act is contrary to the Muslim law."
GIVEN `the Mufti gave evidence it is contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court presumes the doctrine contrary to Muslim law` IF
    `the Mufti gave evidence it is contrary`
